fix(recall): give retrieval its own question tracker (4.6.0)

The first live recall-rewrite event after 4.5.1 was recall-rewrite-skip with reason "query too
short". Every other part of the chain worked - the section left its note, agent/pre-step picked it up
in time for the same turn, the rescue decided to rewrite - and then it was handed an empty string.

The question came from capture.lastUserText, and capture deliberately ignores messages whose
source.kind is not user: durable extraction must never treat an injected prompt as something the
person said. Retrieval has the opposite requirement, and it had borrowed capture's filter. A turn
opened by a harness-injected message still has a question worth searching for, so the section always
missed and the rescue always had nothing to rewrite.

A dedicated per-session tracker now records the newest user/message text without that filter, and
capture is untouched. recall-rewrite-skip also records queryChars - the length, never the text - so
"the section could not see the question" and "the model declined" stay distinguishable without
putting a conversation in the audit log.

Same class as the previous four releases: a component silently doing nothing because a filter was
borrowed from a neighbour with different needs. The difference is that this one was named by its own
first audit line, because the diagnostic was placed where the failure happened.
